# ============================================================
# .gitignore — NYC Taxi Operations Intelligence Platform
# ============================================================
# What is .gitignore?
#   Git tracks every file in your project folder. But some
#   files should NEVER be uploaded to GitHub — credentials,
#   temporary files, large data files, local config. This file
#   tells Git: ignore these files, never track them, never
#   upload them. If a file is listed here, it is invisible
#   to Git even if it sits in your project folder.
# ============================================================


# --- CREDENTIALS (CRITICAL — never commit these) ---
*.json
# Service account key files from Google Cloud are JSON.
# If this file ever gets pushed to GitHub, anyone on the
# internet can access your BigQuery project and run queries
# at your expense. This line prevents that entirely.

.env
# Your .env file stores the path to your credentials and
# your GCP project ID. Never commit it.

credentials/
# A folder where credentials files might be stored locally.


# --- Python Environment ---
venv/
env/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.eggs/
# What these are: when you create a virtual environment
# (venv), Python creates a folder with hundreds of library
# files. These are all auto-generated and can be recreated
# with `pip install -r requirements.txt`. There is no reason
# to store them in Git — they make the repo huge and slow.

# --- Jupyter Notebooks ---
.ipynb_checkpoints/
# Jupyter creates checkpoint files every time you save a
# notebook. They are backups for Jupyter's own use and
# should not be in Git.


# --- Data Files (too large for Git) ---
*.parquet
*.csv
data/
raw_data/
# Parquet files can be hundreds of megabytes each. GitHub
# has a 100MB file size limit and a 1GB repo soft limit.
# We never store raw data in Git. Data lives in BigQuery.
# The ingestion script downloads it fresh when needed.


# --- macOS system files ---
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
# macOS creates hidden .DS_Store files in every folder to
# store folder view settings. These are personal to your
# machine and meaningless to anyone else. Always ignore them.


# --- dbt ---
nyc_taxi_dbt/target/
nyc_taxi_dbt/dbt_packages/
nyc_taxi_dbt/logs/
dbt_project/target/
dbt_project/dbt_packages/
dbt_project/logs/
# dbt generates compiled SQL and logs in these folders when
# it runs. They are outputs, not source code. Ignore them.
# The actual model source files (models/*.sql) ARE committed.

# --- Exported data ---
tableau_data/

# --- Log files ---
logs/
*.log

# --- Internal planning docs ---
MILESTONES.md
ROADMAP.md
PROJECT_BRIEF.md
SETUP_GUIDE.md
ARCHITECTURE.md

# --- Empty placeholder folders ---
dbt_project/
analysis/
dashboards/
*.gitkeep


# --- IDE and editor files ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
# Personal editor settings. What you see in VS Code is your
# own configuration — it should not override someone else's.
